A||||3||Jncomutt||Help!! Car Randomly Stalls.    (kind of long)||||1||
Z||000000||Jncomutt||10-05-2001||05:15 PM||||1984 4cyl. 4 speed:<P>My car started stalling today.  It doesn't do it on startup or when I warm it up and let it idle for any amount of time.  I drove my car for 40 mins on the highway at about 75mph the whole way.  When I was coming off the offramp, I just took my foot off the gas and let it coast, slowing me down.  When I went to give it more gas, there was nothing.  No pedal response.  I pushed in the clutch and the RPMs went right down to zero..  Let the clutch back out and pop started and continued driving.<P>About 3 minutes later on the backroads to my house, I sat at a light, got going, got to 3rd gear, and then as I was going, it just like stopped again..  pushed in the clutch, RPMS dropped to about 200-300 then 3 seconds later kicked up to 1500 and I continued driving.<P>Now I notice this to be happening randomly while I'm driving.  It hasn't happened at WOT and not at idle.  Usually it happens when I take my foot off the gas, let it wind down, then try to go again.<P>Sometime when I push in the clutch it stalls right out.  Other times it will go to about 200rpms then come back up.  I haven't noticed a pattern yet.  It happens about every 3-4 minutes of driving.  Need to locate the problem, this is my daily driver....||||reg||1
Z||000001||normalicy||10-05-2001||06:23 PM||||It's probably either your fuel pump, or your pickup coil/ignition coil overheating.  In either case, they need replacing.  It's hard to pinpoint since it only happens when the car is moving though.<P>------------------<BR>What is normal anyway?||||reg||1
Z||000002||Jncomutt||10-06-2001||03:33 PM||||Well I have an aftermarket MSD GM coil and a 6A module hooked up.  I just put them on about 2 months ago.  Could they still have gone bad??<P>Also, I noticed whenever I start the car back up right after this happens, I Hear a "SQUEAK" for about 1-2 seconds.  This never happens anyother time I start the car.<P>Any further opinions???||||reg||1
Z||000003||johnt671||10-06-2001||05:04 PM||||I have an 84 with and MSD GM coil and 6A system also.  Put them on the car in March and the MSD coil died last month after about 2500 miles.  Even moved the coil off the engine to a cooler spot.  Went with MSD because a lot of people said they had trouble with Accel.  Now I have a $15.00 wells coil on and miss the MSD but can't buy a new coil every 3000 miles.  ||||reg||1
